@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] resume-token-no-elevation-no-diagnostics
The validator MUST not be setuid and MUST NOT print tokens, arguments or library
diagnostics; stderr redirects to /dev/null before the library runs. Stdout is
a fixed result word (`ok\n`) only. Operational events stay with the caller's
Lilly.Events catalog.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] resume-token-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover the bounded token envelope (version, sizes, even
lowercase hex, declared-size bounds) and the lineage matrix (exact name/
toguid/fromguid, key allowlist, duplicate/unknown rejection, boolean-only
capability flags) via an independent spec, plus the canonical `decimal` to
GUID grammar (no sign, padding or leading zero; fits in u64) and the
`parse_cli` selector lattice against independent oracles. Typed FFI to libzfs
MUST be the only unsafe surface; real-token acceptance evidence belongs to the
disposable ZFS transfer fixtures.
